      "side": 1,
      "message": "Throughout bootrom.cc and ec\\_comm.cc, buffers are pre-allocated and timeouts are passed inline:\n\n* std::vector\\\u003cuint8\\_t\\\u003e ret(4096 \\+ kStatusHeaderSize, 0);  \n* std::vector\\\u003cuint8\\_t\\\u003e resp\\_buf(512);  \n* SendBootromCommand(data, current\\_read, 5000ms);  \n* std::this\\_thread::sleep\\_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(800)); (in et171\\_flash.cc)\n\n**The Fix:** Centralize these limits at the top of their respective classes or in a shared config block:\n\n```c\n// In bootrom.h\nclass BootromComm {\n public:\n  static constexpr size_t kMaxPayloadSize \u003d 4096;\n  static constexpr auto kFlashEraseTimeout \u003d std::chrono::milliseconds(5000);\n  // ...\n};\n\n// In ec_comm.h\nclass EcComm {\n public:\n  static constexpr size_t kMaxResponseSize \u003d 512;\n  // ...\n};\n\n```\n\nThen use kMaxPayloadSize \\+ kStatusHeaderSize and kFlashEraseTimeout in the implementation. It immediately tells the reader *why* that specific size or duration was chosen.",
      "revId": "174c19ecb866ee787a77ebc705630b6c2c1577be",
