      "side": 1,
      "message": "**The Problem:** SendBootromCommandRaw, SendBootromCommandSha, and SendBootromCommandAes all duplicate the exact same USB transmission logic, memory allocation, error handling, and status header checking (about 15 lines of identical code in three different places).\n\n**The Fix:** Extract the core USB transmit/receive and status-check loop into a single private helper function inside BootromComm.\n\n**Add this helper to bootrom.cc:**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::DoUsbTransfer(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e tx_cmd, \n    size_t min_expected_rx_size,\n    std::chrono::milliseconds timeout) {\n  \n  DumpRawCmd(tx_cmd);\n\n  if (auto res \u003d usb_.BulkWrite(kBootromEpOutBulk, tx_cmd, timeout); !res)\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kUsbWriteFailed);\n\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e ret(4096 + min_expected_rx_size, 0);\n  auto read_res \u003d usb_.BulkRead(kBootromEpInBulk, ret, timeout);\n  \n  if (!read_res || read_res.value() \u003c\u003d 0)\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kUsbReadFailed);\n\n  ret.resize(read_res.value());\n\n  if (ret.size() \u003c min_expected_rx_size)\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n\n  // All valid Bootrom responses start with a 0x00 0x00 status header\n  if (ret[0] !\u003d 0 || ret[1] !\u003d 0)\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kInvalidStatusHeader);\n\n  return ret;\n}\n\n```\n\nNow, SendBootromCommandSha becomes incredibly clean—it just packs the header and calls the helper:\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e\nBootromComm::SendBootromCommandSha(...) {\n  // ... [Pack the SHA header and append data into `cmd`] ...\n\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, kScHeaderSizeSha, timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n\n  // Return everything after the header\n  return std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(ret_res-\u003ebegin() + kScHeaderSizeSha, ret_res-\u003eend());\n}\n\n```\n\n*(Apply this exact same simplification to the Raw and Aes variants).*",
