      "side": 1,
      "message": "In bootrom.cc, various read/write methods inject 0x04 or 0x01 into the command buffer without any explanation:\n\n```c\n// Old:\nstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e cmd \u003d {EgisBootrom::kCmdMemRead};\nAppendLittleEndian(cmd, addr);\ncmd.push_back(0x04); // What is 0x04?\n\n```\n\nThese appear to be access sizes or memory space identifiers (e.g., 0x04 for Word/Register access, 0x01 for Byte/Flash access).\n\n**The Fix:** Define these inside the EgisBootrom namespace in bootrom.h:\n\n```c\n// In bootrom.h\nnamespace EgisBootrom {\n  constexpr uint8_t kAccessSizeByte \u003d 0x01;\n  constexpr uint8_t kAccessSizeWord \u003d 0x04;\n}\n\n// In bootrom.cc\ncmd.push_back(EgisBootrom::kAccessSizeWord);\n\n```",
