      "side": 1,
      "message": "The DisableWatchdog function in bootrom.cc blasts several unexplained hex values into registers:\n\n```c\n// Old:\nWriteReg(EgisBootrom::kRegPwmCtrl, 0x00000004);\nWriteReg(EgisBootrom::kRegPwmReload, 0x00070a21);\n\n```\n\n**The Fix:** These should be defined as constexpr bitmasks alongside the register addresses in bootrom.h. Even if the exact bitfields aren\u0027t fully documented by the vendor, naming the *entire* payload after its purpose is better than raw hex:\n\n```c\n// In bootrom.h\nconstexpr uint32_t kPwmCtrlDisableMask \u003d 0x00000004;\nconstexpr uint32_t kPwmReloadTimeoutVal \u003d 0x00070a21;\n\n// In bootrom.cc\nWriteReg(EgisBootrom::kRegPwmCtrl, kPwmCtrlDisableMask);\n\n```",
