      "message": "In bootrom.h, the AES key setter accepts a raw byte pointer:\n\n```c\n// Old:\nvoid SetAesKey(const uint8_t *key) {\n  std::memcpy(aes_key_.data(), key, aes_key_.size());\n}\n\n```\n\n**The Risk:** This assumes the caller provides exactly 32 bytes. If the caller accidentally passes a shorter array, memcpy will read out of bounds. **The Fix:** Use a fixed-size std::span to enforce the exact length at compile time.\n\n```c\n// New:\nvoid SetAesKey(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t, 32\u003e key) {\n  std::copy(key.begin(), key.end(), aes_key_.begin());\n}\n\n```",
