      "writtenOn": "2026-05-21T18:39:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here are Gemini generated instructions on how to fix this. Review for correctness.\n\n----\n\n### Step 1: Expose Endian Utilities in bootrom.h\n\nOpen bootrom.h. Add \\#include  to the top includes, and then move AppendLittleEndian and ReadLittleEndian from bootrom.cc into the header file (just before the EgisBootrom namespace).\n\n```c\n// In bootrom.h\n#include \u003cbit\u003e // Add this with the other includes\n\n// Add these utility functions:\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nvoid AppendLittleEndian(std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e \u0026vec, T value) {\n  if constexpr (std::endian::native !\u003d std::endian::little) {\n    value \u003d std::byteswap(value);\n  }\n  auto bytes \u003d std::bit_cast\u003cstd::array\u003cuint8_t, sizeof(T)\u003e\u003e(value);\n  vec.append_range(bytes);\n}\n\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cT, int\u003e ReadLittleEndian(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buffer) {\n  if (buffer.size() \u003c sizeof(T)) return std::unexpected(-1);\n\n  T value;\n  std::memcpy(\u0026value, buffer.data(), sizeof(T));\n\n  if constexpr (std::endian::native !\u003d std::endian::little) {\n    value \u003d std::byteswap(value);\n  }\n  return value;\n}\n\n```\n\n*Note: Make sure to delete these two functions from the anonymous namespace in bootrom.cc.*\n\n### Step 2: Add the ParseError Enum\n\nOpen et171\\_flash.cc. In the anonymous namespace (namespace {) near the top of the file, add the enum and stringifier:\n\n```c\nenum class ParseError {\n  kDataTooSmall,\n  kInvalidHeader,\n  kUnsupportedCrypto,\n  kTruncatedHeader,\n  kInvalidPayloadSize,\n};\n\nconstexpr std::string_view ToString(ParseError err) {\n  switch (err) {\n    case ParseError::kDataTooSmall:\n      return \"Data too small to parse header\";\n    case ParseError::kInvalidHeader:\n      return \"Invalid command header\";\n    case ParseError::kUnsupportedCrypto:\n      return \"Unsupported crypto algorithm\";\n    case ParseError::kTruncatedHeader:\n      return \"Data truncated before full header could be read\";\n    case ParseError::kInvalidPayloadSize:\n      return \"Failed to read payload size\";\n    default:\n      return \"Unknown parsing error\";\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n### Step 3: Create the GetNextPacketSize Helper\n\nStill inside the anonymous namespace in et171\\_flash.cc, add the parsing helper. Notice how it now cleanly calls ReadLittleEndian:\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003csize_t, ParseError\u003e GetNextPacketSize(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e fw) {\n  if (fw.size() \u003c 2) return std::unexpected(ParseError::kDataTooSmall);\n  \n  if (fw[0] \u003d\u003d EgisBootrom::kCmdSystemReset) {\n    return 2; // System Reset is a fixed 2-byte packet\n  }\n  \n  if (fw[0] !\u003d EgisBootrom::kCmdSecureWrapped) {\n    return std::unexpected(ParseError::kInvalidHeader);\n  }\n\n  size_t header_size \u003d 0;\n  EgisCryptoType algo \u003d static_cast\u003cEgisCryptoType\u003e(fw[1]);\n  \n  if (algo \u003d\u003d EgisCryptoType::kSha256) {\n    header_size \u003d BootromComm::kScHeaderSizeSha;\n  } else if (algo \u003d\u003d EgisCryptoType::kAesGcm) {\n    header_size \u003d BootromComm::kScHeaderSizeAes;\n  } else {\n    return std::unexpected(ParseError::kUnsupportedCrypto);\n  }\n\n  if (fw.size() \u003c header_size) {\n    return std::unexpected(ParseError::kTruncatedHeader);\n  }\n\n  // Safely extract the wrapped size using the shared template function\n  auto wrapped_size \u003d ReadLittleEndian\u003cuint32_t\u003e(fw.subspan(2, 4));\n  if (!wrapped_size) {\n    return std::unexpected(ParseError::kInvalidPayloadSize);\n  }\n\n  return header_size + wrapped_size.value();\n}\n\n```\n\n### Step 4: Refactor RunFlashCmd\n\nReplace the implementation of RunFlashCmd with this streamlined version:\n\n```c\nint RunFlashCmd(const AppConfig \u0026config, UsbComm \u0026boot_comm,\n                BootromComm \u0026brom) {\n  if (config.fw_path.empty()) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] -flashcmd requires a command file path.\");\n    return -1;\n  }\n  \n  auto firmware_opt \u003d ReadBinaryFile(config.fw_path);\n  if (!firmware_opt) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Cannot open or read file: {}\", config.fw_path);\n    return -1;\n  }\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e \u0026firmware \u003d firmware_opt.value();\n\n  std::println(\"--- Flash RAW CMD Binary Flashing ---\");\n  size_t done \u003d 0;\n  \n  while (done \u003c firmware.size()) {\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e remaining(firmware.data() + done, firmware.size() - done);\n    \n    // 1. Parse bounds\n    auto packet_size_res \u003d GetNextPacketSize(remaining);\n    if (!packet_size_res) {\n      std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Parse failed at offset 0x{:X}: {}\", \n                   done, ToString(packet_size_res.error()));\n      return -1;\n    }\n    \n    size_t packet_size \u003d packet_size_res.value();\n    \n    // Guard against a packet claiming to be larger than the remaining file size\n    if (packet_size \u003e remaining.size()) {\n       std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Packet truncated at offset 0x{:X}. Expected {} bytes.\", \n                    done, packet_size);\n       return -1;\n    }\n\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e packet \u003d remaining.first(packet_size);\n\n    // 2. Send Data\n    auto res \u003d boot_comm.BulkWrite(BootromComm::kBootromEpOutBulk, packet, kTransferTimeout);\n    if (!res || res.value() !\u003d static_cast\u003cint\u003e(packet.size())) {\n       std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] USB write failed at 0x{:X}: {}\", \n                    done, !res ? ToString(res.error()) : \"Incomplete write\");\n       return -1;\n    }\n\n    // 3. Receive Response (System reset commands do not generate responses)\n    if (packet[0] !\u003d EgisBootrom::kCmdSystemReset) {\n      std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e resp(128, 0);\n      auto read_res \u003d boot_comm.BulkRead(BootromComm::kBootromEpInBulk, resp, kTransferTimeout);\n      if (!read_res || read_res.value() \u003c\u003d 0) {\n        std::println(stderr, \"\\n[ERROR] Device no response at 0x{:X}\", done);\n        return -1;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // 4. Advance and print progress\n    done +\u003d packet_size;\n    std::print(\"\\rFlashing Progress: {} / {} ({:.1f}%)\", done, firmware.size(),\n               (static_cast\u003cfloat\u003e(done) / firmware.size() * 100.0f));\n    std::fflush(stdout);\n  }\n  \n  std::println(\"\\n[OK] RAW CMD Flashing Finished\");\n  if (auto res \u003d brom.SystemReset(); !res) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[WARN] System reset command failed: {}\", ToString(res.error()));\n  }\n  return 0;\n}\n\n```",
